{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794172916,"nonce":"O51fraTFsQ/kFPMTha8FHGk7TrE=","target":"af44a7e5ee258dc6d30ef7e91d88b1adcf573fc0276a0b22eb5a12888090dfbd","message":"## Context\nThe user adds single project dirs or parent dirs to scan; the app must find git repos that use git-bug, fast, and remember what it saw so startup is instant.\n\n## Files\n- `src/workspace.rs` — new, exported from `src/lib.rs`: config + discovery\n- `src/cache.rs` — new, exported from `src/lib.rs`: fingerprints + on-disk snapshot\n\n## Approach\n- `cargo add directories`, `cargo add --dev tempfile`.\n- `Workspace { roots: Vec\u003cRoot\u003e, scan_depth: u8 /* default 4 */, dark: bool }`, `Root { path, kind: Project | Scan }`, serde JSON at `ProjectDirs::from(\"dev\", \"arkye03\", \"gbtracker\")` config dir `/workspace.json`. Missing file → default. Save via temp file + rename.\n- `async discover(\u0026Workspace) -\u003e Vec\u003cRepoInfo { root, name, has_git_bug }\u003e`: dir walk in `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`, roots walked concurrently; git calls concurrent but bounded by a `tokio::sync::Semaphore` (CPU count). `Project` → that dir; `Scan` → walk to `scan_depth`; a dir with `.git` (dir or file) is a repo and is not descended into; skip hidden dirs, `node_modules`, `target`; never follow symlinks.\n- Dedupe by git common dir (`git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir`): git-bug state lives there, shared by linked worktrees (`../skillforge/plugins/roadmap/skills/gb/scripts/lib/gb_core.sh:11-18`).\n- git-bug presence: `git for-each-ref --count=1 refs/bugs refs/identities` non-empty — cheap, takes no git-bug lock.\n- `async fingerprint(root)`: hash of `git for-each-ref refs/bugs --format=%(refname) %(objectname)` — changes on any bug write, costs one git call, no git-bug lock.\n- Snapshot cache at the `ProjectDirs` cache dir: `repos.json` (last discovery) and `issues/\u003chash of common dir\u003e.json` = `{fingerprint, issues}`. `load_snapshot()` returns everything cached; `is_stale(root, cached_fp)` compares fingerprints. Corrupt or version-mismatched cache files are ignored, never fatal.\n\n## Depends on\nL1 — `src/lib.rs`, serializable `Issue`\n\n## Out of scope\n- UI, issue loading.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Tempdir tests: scan finds nested repos up to depth, skips `node_modules` and hidden dirs, stops at repo boundaries, dedupes a linked worktree, and flags git-bug presence after `git update-ref refs/bugs/x HEAD`\n- Fingerprint test: same value twice, different after `git update-ref refs/bugs/y HEAD`\n- Save/load round-trip tests for `workspace.json` and the issue snapshot against temp paths; a corrupt cache file loads as empty\n- All three gates pass","files":null}]}